Description: VMware's alpha cursor pseudo-encoding
 The Cursor pseudo-encoding (-239) has a one-bit mask, so a cursor's
 translucent pixels (a soft shadow, a translucent fill) are either dropped or
 made opaque. VMware's cursor pseudo-encoding (0x574d5664) with cursor type 1
 carries each pixel's R, G, B and straight alpha bytes. noVNC asks for it
 before Cursor and decodes it in _handleVMwareCursor; TigerVNC's viewer reads
 it too. A client that asks for it gets the cursor that way, any other the
 Cursor pseudo-encoding as before. The test server gets a 2x1 cursor, and the
 handshake tests check both encodings of it. neatvnc.h defines
 NVNC_HAS_VMWARE_ALPHA_CURSOR for programs to tell this build from others.
Author: Mariotaku <git@mariotaku.me>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-26
